_🚀 Performance & Scalability_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Memoize locale discovery during refresh chunks.**

Line 526 calls `get_site_locales()` for every plugin in a chunk, and that helper scans users plus all sites. On larger multisite installs this can turn one cron chunk into repeated full-network scans.





<details>
<summary>⚡ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
     private function get_site_locales(): array {
+        static $cached_locales = null;
+        if (null !== $cached_locales) {
+            return $cached_locales;
+        }
+
         $locales = [get_locale()];

         $user_ids = get_users(['fields' => 'ID']);
         foreach ($user_ids as $user_id) {
             $user_locale = get_user_meta((int) $user_id, 'locale', true);
@@

         $locales = array_values(array_filter(array_unique($locales)));

-        return empty($locales) ? ['en_US'] : $locales;
+        $cached_locales = empty($locales) ? ['en_US'] : $locales;
+
+        return $cached_locales;
     }
```

</details>


Also applies to: 651-680

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the
rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.

In `@src/class-translation-manager.php` around lines 525 - 527, The
`get_site_locales()` method is being called repeatedly within the
`get_needed_translations()` function for each plugin processed in a chunk,
causing expensive full-network scans on large multisite installations. To fix
this, memoize the result of `get_site_locales()` by calling it once at the
beginning and storing the result in a variable, then reuse that cached variable
throughout the method instead of making repeated calls. This optimization should
be applied both to the call at the start of `get_needed_translations()` method
and also to the related code section referenced at lines 651-680.
```

</details>

